FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/runtime.rs:3554 — the message arm matches `[message]` for any `Value` and calls `message.to_string()`, so `logging.info(5)` (or a list/record/`nothing`) silently logs a coerced string. This contradicts the documented signature `logging.info(text)` at src/stdlib.rs:2449 and the REPORT's claim that "wrong argument types ... are catchable `Runtime` errors"; `edge_invalid_levels_and_destinations_are_refused` tests `logging.info()` (arity) but never a wrong-typed message. Fix: require `Value::Text` for the message (or explicitly document coercion) and add a test for `logging.info(5)`.

2. [MINOR] src/wasm.rs:941 — `edge_an_unrelated_thread_is_not_part_of_an_open_capture` never opens a capture and never calls `is_capturing`/`try_emit`; it only checks that a thread-local does not leak into a fresh thread. It would stay green if `is_capturing()` at src/wasm.rs:109 ignored `capture_member()` entirely, so the newly added false branch of `capture_member() && CAPTURING` has no real test. Fix: call `begin_capture()` on one thread, then from an unrelated thread assert `is_capturing()` is false and `try_emit` reaches the real stream while `CAPTURED` stays unchanged.

3. [MINOR] src/logging.rs:123 — `format_timestamp()` returns `None` when `current_instant()` fails, so on a wasm host that has not called `rb_set_clock` a record emitted with `timestamps == true` silently loses its timestamp and becomes indistinguishable from `set_timestamps(no)`. SPEC's logging section states timestamps are on by default and that the record shape is `[timestamp] [LEVEL] message`; the no-clock fallback is documented only in a code comment and the phase report, not in SPEC. Fix: either document the no-clock fallback in SPEC or emit a defined placeholder/error so "on" and "off" remain distinguishable.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 3
